     docs/detached-bodies-and-archive-profile.1.0.md? The normative points: (1) 
     a general-claim's content may carry {media_type, body_b3, body_len} instead
     of {media_type, body} — exactly one of body/body_b3 must be present, both 
     or neither is not well-formed; (2) body status is a three-state judgment 
     separate from attestation validity: verified / absent / mismatched, never 
     folded into signature failure; (3) the preservation stance is normative — 
     mismatched bytes are retained, reported loudly, and stay exportable; never 
     deleted or silently repaired. → Ratify as specified (Recommended)

